<p>At the Munich Security Conference in Germany, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said any peace agreement must start with strong, long-term US security guarantees. In his view, credible protection has to come first for any deal to hold. He also pushed for a clearer path toward EU membership as part of any settlement Ukraine could accept, including a more defined timeline for accession.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/YpUTIXdEOR35DSwn5yiFLGA1mTisU6jLEF868ycEx7qsUSSDMSKOZK4HS4TGu8VcMwi7CoP1hurbIKD1Bo-R9jSvsVS_15sFaNrZzqQbVYPWWi16kcds4K7Auk5tyf4oZ0SaS60r5oPSfZtq-onqEsrlSczXqgGz2s0atWi1NN5_4OlqbyfF73vjVAGO8eVkKbVk82ZW32WTVv_nMyktZHQqsxlVfGwWmdWzXjrLa3Ia_WoOIi1wnDqwtLoHrULo07LR' alt='Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy speaks during the Munich Security Conference.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Energy damage (attributed claim): Zelenskyy said Russian attacks have damaged every power plant in Ukraine, highlighting the strain on civilian infrastructure as winter conditions persist.</li><li>Negotiating shake-up: Zelenskyy said he was surprised that Moscow replaced the head of its negotiating team ahead of another round of U.S.-brokered talks.</li><li>EU timeline detail: Zelenskyy called for a clear date for Ukraine to be allowed to join the EU; some EU officials have suggested it could be as early as 2027.</li><li>Praise for allies: Speaking to reporters, Zelenskyy repeatedly thanked Americans and Europeans for their support.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy (Ukraine): He said peace remains out of reach and urged allies to speed up weapons deliveries to Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-zelenskyy-at-msc-putin-is-a-slave-to-war/a-75973922'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy (Ukraine): He said Ukraine wants a legally binding US security guarantee for at least 20 years and urged the EU to set a clear accession date. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/14/ukraine-wants-20-year-us-security-guarantee-to-sign-peace-deal'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy (Ukraine): He criticized what he described as a pattern in which the United States asks Kyiv, rather than Moscow, for concessions during negotiations. (<a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/zelenskiy-says-us-too-often-asks-ukraine-not-russia-for-concessions3'>Japan Today</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-zelenskyy-at-msc-putin-is-a-slave-to-war/a-75973922'>Ukraine&#x27;s Zelenskyy at MSC: Putin is a &#x27;slave to war&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c4a0a5e7-1678-4303-b621-a447bca69d64'>Zelenskyy insists elections can only take place two months after a ceasefire</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/14/ukraine-wants-20-year-us-security-guarantee-to-sign-peace-deal'>Ukraine wants 20-year US security guarantee to sign peace deal</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/zelenskyy-says-questions-remain-in-peace-talks-over-security-guarantees-for-ukraine'>Zelenskyy says questions remain in peace talks over security guarantees for Ukraine</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/zelenskiy-says-us-too-often-asks-ukraine-not-russia-for-concessions3'>Zelenskyy says U.S. too often asks Ukraine, not Russia, for concessions</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/zelenskyy-says-putin-is-slave-to-war-as-he-demands-security-guarantees-at-munich-conference-13979895.html'>Zelenskyy says Putin is &#x27;slave to war&#x27; as he demands security guarantees at Munich conference</a> - firstpost.com</li></ul>